                <pb facs="0859" n="715" sameAs="frus:frus1929v02/pg715"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.05/182: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >MacMurray</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peiping</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-11-18T16:00:00+08:00">November 18, 1929—4
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 9:20 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>1004. Legation’s 1000, November 14, 8 p.m. Following telegram has been received
                    from Jacobs and Bucknell: “Pending further instructions from Legation, we shall
                    not proceed to Nanking. Similar action is being taken by other delegates”, which
                    I have telegraphically approved.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">MacMurray</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
